.TH "SERIAL" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Serial \- Serial
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[CR]Serial\f[R] interface of the Web Serial API provides
attributes and methods for finding and connecting to serial ports from a
web page.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
.TP
\f[B]Serial.requestPort()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an instance of
\f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] representing the device chosen by the user.
This method must be called via transient activation.
.TP
\f[B]Serial.getPorts()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an array of
\f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] objects representing serial ports connected to the
host which the origin has permission to access.
.SH EVENTS
The following events are available to \f[CR]Serial\f[R] via event
bubbling from \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]:
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort\f[R] \f[B]connect\f[R] event
An event fired when a port has been connected to the device.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort\f[R] \f[B]disconnect\f[R] event
An event fired when a port has been disconnected from the device.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example shows how a site can check for available ports and
allow the user to grant it permission to access additional ports.
.PP
On load event listeners are added for the \f[CR]connect\f[R] and
\f[CR]disconnect\f[R] events so that the site can react when a device is
connected or disconnected from the system.
The \f[CR]getPorts()\f[R] method is then called to see which ports are
connected that the site already has access to.
.PP
If the site doesn\(cqt have access to any connected ports it has to wait
until it has user activation to proceed.
In this example we use a \f[CR]click\f[R] event handler on a button for
this task.
A filter is passed to \f[CR]requestPort()\f[R] with a USB vendor ID in
order to limit the set of devices shown to the user to only USB devices
built by a particular manufacturer.
.IP
.EX
navigator.serial.addEventListener(\(dqconnect\(dq, (e) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// Connect to \(gae.target\(ga or add it to a list of available ports.\f[R]
});

navigator.serial.addEventListener(\(dqdisconnect\(dq, (e) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// Remove \(gae.target\(ga from the list of available ports.\f[R]
});

navigator.serial.getPorts().then((ports) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// Initialize the list of available ports with \(gaports\(ga on page load.\f[R]
});

button.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] usbVendorId = 0xabcd;
  navigator.serial
    .requestPort({ filters: [{ usbVendorId }] })
    .then((port) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
      \f[I]// Connect to \(gaport\(ga or add it to the list of available ports.\f[R]
    })
    .catch((e) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
      \f[I]// The user didn\(aqt select a port.\f[R]
    });
});
.EE
